    metric Components Modal "The classic modal component with graceful spacings across devices and viewports, using the semantic HTML tag <dialog>."
    col
      text Content
      link Syntax /docs/modal
      link Demo /docs/modal#demo
      link Utilities /docs/modal#utilities
    col
      text Modals are built with <dialog> as a wrapper and <article> for the modal content.
      text "Inside <header> <button rel=\"prev\"> is defined to float: right; allowing a close icon to be top aligned with a title."
      card
        button Close
        text 🗓️ Thank You for Registering!
      text We’re excited to have you join us for our upcoming event. Please arrive at the museum on time to check in and get started.
      text Date: Saturday, April 15
      text "Time: 10:00am - 12:00pm"
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/modal
        text "<dialog open> <article> <header> <button aria-label=\"Close\" rel=\"prev\"></button> <p> <strong>🗓️ Thank You for Registering!</strong> </p> </header> <p> We're excited to have you join us for our upcoming event. Please arrive at the museum on time to check in and get started. </p> <ul> <li>Date: Saturday, April 15</li> <li>Time: 10:00am - 12:00pm</li> </ul> </article> </dialog>"
      text Inside <footer>, the content is right aligned by default.
      h2 Confirm Your Membership
      text Thank you for signing up for a membership! Please review the membership details below:
      text Membership: Individual
      text Price: $10
      row
        button Cancel primary
        button Confirm primary
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/modal
        text "<dialog open> <article> <h2>Confirm Your Membership</h2> <p> Thank you for signing up for a membership! Please review the membership details below: </p> <ul> <li>Membership: Individual</li> <li>Price: $10</li> </ul> <footer> <button class=\"secondary\"> Cancel </button> <button>Confirm</button> </footer> </article> </dialog>"
      h2 Demo#
      text Toggle a modal by clicking the button below.
      button "Open modal" primary
      text Pico does not include JavaScript code. You need to implement your JS to interact with modals.
      link HTMLDialogElement https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLDialogElement
      link "Vanilla JavaScript" https://codesandbox.io/embed/4mrnhq?view=Editor+%2B+Preview&module=%2Fjs%2Fmodal.js
      link React https://codesandbox.io/p/devbox/github/picocss/examples/tree/master/v2-react-color-schemes-and-modal?embed=1&file=%2Fsrc%2Fcomponents%2FModal.js
      text To open a modal, add the open attribute to the<dialog> container.
      h2 Utilities#
      text Modals come with 3 utility classes.
      link "class-less version" /docs/classless
      text .modal-is-open prevents any scrolling and interactions below the modal.
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/modal
        text "<!doctype html> <html class=\"modal-is-open\"> ... </html>"
      text .modal-is-opening brings an opening animation.
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/modal
        text "<!doctype html> <html class=\"modal-is-open modal-is-opening\"> ... </html>"
      text .modal-is-closing brings a closing animation.
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/modal
        text "<!doctype html> <html class=\"modal-is-open modal-is-closing\"> ... </html>"
      link "Edit this page on GitHub" https://github.com/picocss/picocss.com/blob/main/app/routes/docs.modal.jsx
  col
